      "overall": "PSG host Bayern in the UCL semi-final first leg as defending champions and slight market favourites at home, but Bayern have a remarkable recent edge in this fixture - Bayern have won each of their last five Champions League games against the French giants, the longest winning streak any team has achieved against PSG in major European competition, including a 2-1 win at Parc des Princes in early November in the league phase courtesy of two first-half Luis Diaz goals before he was sent off. Both teams are elite attacking units - with 38 goals each in the competition this season, the most of any clubs. PSG come in fresher having rested players in the 3-0 win over Angers, while Bayern needed a frantic 4-3 comeback at Mainz with only two days recovery. Key absences: Bayern miss Guerreiro, Gnabry, Ulreich and head coach Kompany who is suspended for yellow card accumulation; PSG sweat over Vitinha's fitness while Ndjantou is sidelined. Opta's pre-match simulation gives PSG winning the first leg in 41.1% of pre-match simulations, which aligns with bookmaker pricing of PSG ~+130, Draw +280, Bayern +175. Open, high-event match expected.",
